      {=hec.rss.model.ReservoirElement
        ID=3570
        FLD=_index
        I=93
        FLD=_name
        STR=Detroit
        FLD=_description
        STR=Detroit Dam and Lake (North Santiam River).  Detroit Lake near Detroit, OR.  USGS gage 14180500;  NWS RFC ID DETO3.  RM 60.9, DA=437 sq.mi.  Located 4.9 mi. west of Detroit.  USACE storage project authorized for Flood Control, Power, Navigation, and Irrigation.  Other uses include Fishery, Water Quality, and Recreation.Spillway Rating Table from WM Troll Page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Spillway/DET_Spillway_Rating_Table_Oct2012.xlsm?d=w77c8b71c9cb64d49a9bbd5b57361467f*** Uses free spill curve. Overestimates controlled flow capacity, but good for ResSim.Upper RO rating table from WM Troll Page: https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/_layouts/15/WopiFrame.aspx?sourcedoc={27DC0B61-B950-4A38-938B-3F22889BAA15}&file=Detroit_1RO_CHART_CALCULATOR.xlsx&action=default*** Table extrapolated down to accomidate deep drawdown. Lower elevations not considered in original rating table.Lower RO rating table from WM Troll Page:file:///C:/Users/g2encjer/AppData/Local/Temp/1/MicrosoftEdgeDownloads/d2d8a2b7-f5a5-402b-8c77-e1b7a730505e/DET_LowerRO_Scanned.pdfThe ResSim curve extends below the scanned Lower RO table. the Lower RO table is old and the outlet is rarely used but maybe be used more in the future. Capacity needs to be investigated further.Power Plant capacity provided by April Bardy - Spreadsheet is in shared folder. Actual capacity vs operating capacity may differ slightly. Outlet modeled as controlled outlet and not penstock because post processing of outlet allocations makes power calculations incorrect.
