      {=hec.rss.model.ReservoirElement
        ID=4349
        FLD=_index
        I=98
        FLD=_name
        STR=Foster
        FLD=_description
        STR=Foster Dam and Lake (South Santiam River).  Foster Lake at Foster, OR.  USGS gage 14186600;  NWS RFC ID FOS.  RM 37.7, DA=492 sq.mi.  Located 0.5 mi. north of Foster.  USACE storage project authorized for Flood Control, Power, Navigation, and Irrigation.  Other uses include Fishery, Water Quality, and Recreation.Power Plant capacity provided by April Bardy - - Spreadsheet is in shared folder. Actual capacity vs operating capacity may differ slightly. Outlet modeled as controlled outlet and not penstock because post processing of outlet allocations makes power calculations incorrect. Spillway Rating Table from WM Troll Page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Spillway/FOS_Spillway_Rating_Table_Dec2017.xlsm?d=wbe98c45558b94a0cb04be414b474817d*** Uses free spill curve. Overestimates controlled flow capacity, but good for ResSim.Ryan Cahill edit, 11Dec2025Entries for elevation-storage, release capacity extended to include arbitrarily large point at 699.99 feet.This extension was necessary for FRM operations with high flow, ResSim was getting confused and thinking the pool might rise above top of dam.Real top of dam elevation is 646 ft project datum
