      {=hec.rss.model.ReservoirElement
        ID=5783
        FLD=_index
        I=108
        FLD=_name
        STR=Fern Ridge
        FLD=_description
        STR=Fern Ridge Dam and Lake (Long Tom River).  Fern Ridge Lake near Elmira, OR.  USGS gage 14168000;  NWS RFC ID FRNO3.  RM 25.7, DA=252 sq.mi.  Located 4.5 mi. northeast of Elmira.  USACE storage project authorized for Flood Control, Irrigation, and Navigation.  Other uses include Fishery, Water Quality, and Recreation.RO Rating curve from WM Troll page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Regulating_Outlet/Fern_Ridge_1RO_CHART_CALCULATOR.xlsx?d=wf6cf2a7588f84ad080ebcd3114028eaaFull open rating curve used - minimum gate openings not reflected in rating table.Spillway rating curve from WM Troll page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Spillway/FRN_Spillway_Rating_Table_Oct2012.xlsm?d=w081b58cf95e44bee8207a711b906bf96Free spill curve used which overestimates gated spill, but good for ResSim. Minimum gate openings not reflected in rating table.Sluicegate rating curve from WM Troll page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Regulating_Outlet/FERN-RIDGE_SLUICEgate.pdfMin gate openings not reflected in rating curve. Not sure what the purpose of this outlet is.
