      {=hec.rss.model.ReservoirElement
        ID=6890
        FLD=_index
        I=118
        FLD=_name
        STR=Cougar
        FLD=_description
        STR=Cougar Dam and Lake (South Fork McKenzie River).  Cougar Lake near Rainbow, OR.  USGS gage 14159400;  NWS RFC ID CGRO3.  RM 4.5, DA=207 sq.mi.  Located 2.7 mi. south of Rainbow.  USACE storage project authorized for Flood Control, Power, Navigation, and Irrigation.  Other uses include Fishery, Water Quality, and Recreation.Power Plant capacity provided by April Bardy - Spreadsheet is in shared folder. Actual capacity vs operating capacity may differ slightly. Outlet modeled as controlled outlet and not penstock because post processing of outlet allocations makes power calculations incorrect.RO rating from WM Troll Page: https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Regulating_Outlet/Cougar_1RO_CHART_CALCULATOR.xlsx?d=w8684b75addbc4cb693919db21faa5e08Curve not defined below 1510' so simple linear decrease to invert used. Minimum gate openings not reflected in rating curve.Spillway rating from WM Troll Page: https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Spillway/CGR_Spillway_Rating_Table_Oct2012.xlsm?d=w9005fee30d0e423b9a6036a318b7322bFree flow used which overestimates gated capacity, but good for ResSim - Minimum gate openings not reflected - CGR spillway is not used unless in emergency as the spillway chute is overgrown and has a road.Diversion tunnel rating curve from EIS used, which was taken from the CGR 2.0 study. Rating table could use more verification, but table on WM Troll Page isn't useful.
        FLD=_system
        REF=0
