      {=hec.rss.model.ReservoirElement
        ID=10562
        FLD=_index
        I=148
        FLD=_name
        STR=Hills Creek
        FLD=_description
        STR=Hills Creek Dam and Lake (Middle Fork Willamette River).  Hills Creek Lake near Oakridge, OR.  USGS gage 14145100;  NWS RFC ID HCRO3.  RM 252.5, DA=389 sq.mi.  Located 3.5 mi. southeast of Oakridge.  USACE storage project authorized for Flood Control, Power, Navigation, and Irrigation.  Other uses include Fishery, Water Quality, and Recreation.Power Plant capacity provided by April Bardy -  Spreadsheet is in shared folder. Actual capacity vs operating capacity may differ slightly. Outlet modeled as controlled outlet and not penstock because post processing of outlet allocations makes power calculations incorrect.Spillway rating curve from WM Troll page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Spillway/HCR_Spillway_Rating_Table_Oct2012.xlsm?d=wa453e015164f4fd38ffc6b142d2a5af2Free flow curve used which overestimates gated capacity, but good for ResSim - gate opening restrictions not reflected.RO Rating curve from WM Troll page:https://team.usace.army.mil/sites/NWP/EC/H/water_mgmt/Outlet%20Rating%20Tables/Regulating_Outlet/Hills_Creek_1RO_CHART_CALCULATOR.xlsx?d=w5c8a03b393854575acdea9a6b8bf7eaeGates full open - gate opening requirements not reflected.
